@@@ forum-045
type: forum_thread
title: PROJECT LANTERN — read this before you decide
author: junebug
date: 1999-09-12T01:14:00-07:00
path: /forum/signals/thread_045.html
role: herring
links: /~junebug/lantern.html
---
[junebug | 09/12/99 01:14]
ok so hear me out. Everyone is asking WHO is transmitting on 2182 from a station that's been dead since 1987. I think I know.
There's a Navy relay site 9 miles inland from Cape Sorrow. I found it on a 1972 topo map. It's not on the new maps. In the 70s it was part of something called LANTERN (I found the word in a library book about cold war coastal radar, page 211, I can scan it).
"The light is out" is a CODE PHRASE. Four seven is a station number. Someone switched something back on.
Full writeup on my page: /~junebug/lantern.html
Also: the access road got closed THIS YEAR. coincidence?

[saltmarsh | 09/12/99 08:40]
Jun, the road is closed because it fell into the sea. I posted a photo.

[qrp_anna | 09/12/99 09:15]
I love you Jun but "a word in a library book" is not a signal log. Rule 1.

[junebug | 09/12/99 10:02]
rule 1 is how they get you to stop looking

[keeper | 09/12/99 11:30]
Let's keep it friendly. Jun, post the scan when you have it. Everyone else, more logs on 2182 please.

@@@ forum-046
type: forum_thread
title: Cape Sorrow — some doubts
author: hvale
date: 1999-09-20T20:30:00-07:00
path: /forum/signals/thread_046.html
role: herring
---
[hvale | 09/20/99 20:30]
I have listened to CS-0903 about forty times now. I'll say it plainly because nobody else will. I don't believe it.
1. The voice is too clean. 2182 at night from a dead station with no antenna maintenance in twelve years should sound like soup. This sounds like it was recorded in a room.
2. The procedure is wrong for 1999. "Cape Sorrow radio, the light is out" is how a station talked in the seventies, not now.
3. Lou sat in Florence three nights and heard nothing. Florence is closer.
I'm not accusing anyone of anything. I'm saying rule 1.

[eward | 09/20/99 21:02]
You weren't there, Henrik. I was. You can doubt me all you like but the file is the file.

[junebug | 09/20/99 21:15]
"recorded in a room" ... or transmitted from a modern site using an old script. LANTERN.

[hvale | 09/20/99 22:40]
Jun, please.

[eward | 09/21/99 00:11]
I'm not going to defend myself against a man who has never once left his house to log anything.

[hvale | 09/24/99 18:05]
I've been a member here since 1997 and I won't be part of whatever this is turning into. I'm removing my posts and my page. Mara, Ray, thank you for everything. 73.
▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ [3 posts in this thread were deleted by their author]

